The ios-build branch had drifted: the last real commit was 519b098
(2026-05-11), while ~2 months of iOS work lived only as uncommitted
working-tree edits (backed up as parent-repo patches/*.patch). This
restores real submodule history for all of it. Groups by milestone:

S0 TLS stack (parent 2527f00):
  dlls/secur32/schannel_gnutls.c  — GnuTLS schannel backend hooks
  dlls/ws2_32/unixlib.c           — iOS wineserver INET poll fix

rpcss / real COM milestone (parent dbebbd1):
  dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64.c       — aarch64 SEH unwind pool→PE reverse-
                                    translate (all native __TRY/__EXCEPT
                                    was spinning forever without it)
  dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c     — EC-side reverse-translate hook
  dlls/ntdll/unwind.c, loader.c, ntdll.spec — plumbing/exports
  dlls/combase/rpc.c              — start_rpcss SCM-boot retry
  programs/services/services.c    — respect SERVICE_DISABLED for root
                                    PnP services (upstream winebus bug)
  server/winstation.c             — desktop auto-close suppressed under
                                    WINE_IOS (+ earlier S2 desktop input)

task #21 desktop-freeze-on-child-exit (2026-07-08):
  dlls/win32u/window.c            — get_shared_window freed-object guard
                                    (id==0 → break the STATUS_PENDING loop
                                    instead of spinning under user_lock)

Going forward: commit wine changes here directly; patches/*.patch revert
to human-readable references rather than the load-bearing backup.

(cherry picked from commit d19b1d24a4a6700841e47cd4b628ef9f6b363adc)
